messages:
alex: Ok team — kicking off POC with Marlowe (enterprise). Goal: validate integration for in-product chat assistant + embeddings search. Need to align success criteria, auth, quotas, and streaming behavior.

maria_se: Quick list I think we need: 1) success criteria (latency/cost/quality), 2) sample prompts + eval harness, 3) auth flow (OIDC or API key + IP allowlist), 4) rate limits & burst plan, 5) streaming vs non-streaming behavior, 6) telemetry/events to send.

ben_sales: Customer asks about pricing for the POC — do we do usage credits or temporary dev key? Also they asked if we can cap spend at $500 for trial month.

alex: Offer a capped trial key with quota enforcement + billing hold at cap. Ben, I'll give you the exact policy text. Maria, can we ensure SDK examples show how to check quota errors?

maria_se: Yup — SDK surfaces 429 with x-rate-limit headers. Suggest including sample retry/backoff snippet. Also provide streaming example (they want progressive tokens in UI).

samir_eng: For streaming + retries here's the minimal pattern we recommend in JS:
```js
// setup: Authorization: Bearer <POC_KEY>
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference-sdk';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.POC_KEY });

async function streamChat() {
  const stream = await client.chat.stream({ model: 'redwood-large', prompt: 'Summarize...', max_tokens: 512 });
  for await (const chunk of stream) {
    // update UI with chunk.text
  }
}
// Simple retry on 429 with exponential backoff
async function retryWithBackoff(fn, attempts=3){
  let delay = 300;
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try{ return await fn(); } catch(e){ if(e.code===429) { await sleep(delay); delay *= 2; } else throw e; }
  }
}
```

maria_se: Also include server-side note: validate webhook signature when using streaming callbacks.

julie_security: From security — we need SOC2 controls confirmed, data retention policy for logs, ability to disable caching for PII, and option to route traffic to their VPC (Private) if they proceed to enterprise. Also require an IP allowlist for POC key and encrypted-at-rest confirmation.

alex: Noted. For POC we can: enable no-cache mode, provide short-lived keys (24h or revocable), add IP allowlist, and share SOC2 attestation doc. Julie, can you attach the answers to their security questionnaire by EOD?

julie_security: I’ll draft responses and attach SOC2 + encryption docs. Quick Q: do we persist prompts for eval telemetry by default? Need a toggle.

samir_eng: Telemetry defaults to aggregated metrics. We can add an opt-in raw prompt logging field per-POC (requires consent). Will provide endpoint for event ingestion: POST /poc/events with minimal schema.

ben_sales: Customer success criteria from Marlowe: 1) p95 latency < 600ms for short chat turns, 2) retrieval relevance > 0.65 in their eval scripts, 3) no more than 2 retries per request, 4) visual streaming without large token gaps. They also want a walkthrough by Wed next week.

alex: Ok set of criteria. Action items: Maria — create prompt+eval harness and share a small dataset by Mon. Samir — add SDK snippet + webhook example and the rate-limit headers (x-rate-limit-limit, x-rate-limit-remaining, x-rate-limit-reset). Julie — security questionnaire answers + SOC2. Ben — confirm POC spend cap and send trial key. I’ll schedule the walkthrough.

maria_se: Uploading eval harness draft: https://redwood.internal/poc/marlowe/evals (private link) — includes 40 prompt pairs and pass/fail script.

deploy-bot: Deployment complete: feature/poc-telemetry -> staging (build 1187). :rocket:

samir_eng: Note on quotas: we default POC to 20 req/s with burst to 80 for 30s, and token cap 2M tokens/day. We can tune lower if Marlowe wants. Also return headers like:
```
x-rate-limit-limit: 20
x-rate-limit-remaining: 18
x-rate-limit-reset: 164s
```

ben_sales: That quota looks fine. I'll confirm the $500 cap against those limits.

alex: Great. If nobody objects, I'll mark the thread as the official POC checklist and move updates to the Jira ticket. We'll reconvene after Maria's harness arrives. :+1:
